      <div type="commentary">
        <p n="1">The framed manuscript page number [ⲓⲑ] is printed with a bar above and below as the frame, not as a supralinear stroke.</p>
        <p n="3">The editors note the end of the line perhaps read ϭⲁⲡϥ (apparatus).</p>
        <p n="4">The editors print "leer" (empty) for the space before ⲓⲟⲩⲇⲁⲥ; it is encoded as a blank (vac.).</p>
        <p n="6">Between ⲣⲉϥϩⲱⲧⲃⲉ and the restoration the editors print "Rest abgerieben" (the rest rubbed off); no text is given for it.</p>
        <p n="7">After the three dots the edition opens a bracket, leaves a wide blank (a lost portion of uncounted extent), and closes with the restoration ⲉⲕⲕⲗⲏ at the right; the restoration continues as ⲥⲓⲁ at the start of l. 8.</p>
        <p n="10">The bracket at the line end is not closed in the edition; it is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="11">The glyph of ⲯ in ⲁⲡⲟⲕⲁⲗⲩⲯⲓⲥ is printed cross-shaped (resembling ϯ); the restoration [ⲕⲁⲗⲩ] confirms the word. The bracket at the line end is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="12">The bracket at the line end is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="13">After ⲥ the editors print "Rest abgerieben" (the rest rubbed off); no text is given for it.</p>
        <p n="14">The bracket at the line end is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="15">The bracket at the line end is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="16">The bracket at the line end is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="17">The bracket at the line end is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="18">The bracket at the line end is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="19">The bracket at the line end is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="20">The bracket after ⲙⲛ is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="21">The editors print "leer" (empty) for the space after ⲧⲏⲣⲟⲩ; it is encoded as a blank (vac.).</p>
        <p n="22">The bracket at the line end is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="24">The editors note that the overline expected over ⲥ̄ⲏ̄ⲣ̄ is not visible (apparatus: "kein übergesetzter Strich zu sehen"); it is left unmarked.</p>
        <p n="28">The editors print "leer" (empty) for the space; it is encoded as a blank (vac.).</p>
        <p n="29">The editors note the ⲱ of ⲟⲩⲱⲛϩ is written above the line (apparatus: "ⲱ über der Zeile"); encoded as an addition above.</p>
        <p n="31">The editors note ⲱⲃ perhaps read ϣⲃ (apparatus: "viell. ϣⲃ").</p>
        <p n="34">The editors mark ϣⲏⲛ (in ⲙⲡⲓϣⲏⲛ) as quite doubtful (apparatus: "ganz zweifelhaft").</p>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
